          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "സൂചി (sūci) — \"a needle\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sanskrit sūcī, from a root about piercing and pointing, and the same root gives Sanskrit its word for an indication or a sign."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "So the needle and the pointer come from one idea: the thing that goes in, and the thing that points out. A Malayalam newsreader saying that a report indicates something is standing on this root."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "With nūlŭ through the eye of it, a സൂചി (sūci) is what turns cloth back into something a person can wear."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "സൂചി (sūci) from Sanskrit sūcī, \"needle\", taken over whole as a tatsama (CDIAL 13551)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three."
            }
          ]
        },
