          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "മുറം (muṟaṁ) — \"a winnowing tray\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Native Dravidian: a flat plaited tray with a lip on three sides, woven from bamboo strip like the mat and the basket before it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Its work needs the wind. Grain is tossed up off the മുറം (muṟaṁ) and kāṟṟŭ carries the husk sideways while the heavy part drops back — a machine with no moving parts, run on weather."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Ari, the raw rice on the kitchen shelf, has been through one of these on its way there."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "മുറം (muṟaṁ) is native Dravidian, one word with Tamil muṟam and Kannada moṟa (DEDR 5005)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five, and every one of them came off somebody's hands: rope, thread, a needle, a broom and a winnowing tray."
            }
          ]
        },
